            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE_WITH_MESSAGE_UPDATE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 18,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Since it's a patch touching core logic of EM, it would be nice to test it independently in both happy path and error path with/without cached configuration with full debug logs.\n\ni don't think it's some trivial refactoring which can just be grouped together with other stuff. Maybe others will think differently."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 18,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Done, will update commit message."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/perform_scan.cpp",
                    "line": 559,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "see cpp core guidelines on function size. This function is already plenty unreadable,\nlet's not add extra stuff on top here without first breaking something out."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/perform_scan.cpp",
                    "line": 559,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "I agree the function is large but I think the refactor should be done independent of this series - I will still do that but in a different commit. I did separate out a function for what I added below."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/perform_scan.cpp",
                    "line": 634,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "```\nauto nameIt = config.find(\"Name\");\nif (nameIt != config.end() && nameIt->is_string())\n```\n\nIMO it's not appropriate to check if a configuration has a `Name` property (and which type it is) in the middle of the entity-manager probe / scan code.\n\n\nIt's necessary property for both EM config and individual exposes records.\n\nThat's something which should be checked as part of configuration parsing when entity-manager starts and loads (cached) configuration / state.\n\n\nOtherwise we may be checking it multiple times at runtime (on every properties changed and retry of probe and scan), creating extra overhead and i also don't see any proper error messages or testing of the error path here in case the property is not present.\n\n\nIf we instead check it as part of configuration parsing / init flow it will only be done once and we have a clean way to handle it (with proper error message) by discarding that cached configuration or configuration file."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/perform_scan.cpp",
                    "line": 634,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "see cpp core guidelines on function size. Let's break out a function before adding all this extra code in here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/perform_scan.cpp",
                    "line": 634,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Removed the check (checks on Name exist already)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/perform_scan.cpp",
                    "line": 634,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "I agree the function is large but I think the refactor should be done independent of this series - I will still do that but in a different commit. I did separate out a function for what I added below."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/perform_scan.cpp",
                    "line": 638,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Let's add a unit test for the expected state of `passedProbe` + `_missingConfigurations`\n\nIf we need a full paragraph to explain how it works, let's make sure it does not break again in the future."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/perform_scan.cpp",
